surface":"இன்றி","parts":[{"text":"இன்றி","lemma":"iṉṟi","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வெண்குடை","parts":[{"text":"வெண்குடை","lemma":"வெண்குடை","gloss":"white royal umbrella"}],"gloss":"white royal umbrella","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நிழற்றிய","parts":[{"text":"நிழற்றிய","lemma":"niḻaṟṟu","gloss":"shaded"}],"gloss":"that shaded"},{"surface":"ஒருமையோர்க்கும்","parts":[{"text":"ஒருமை","lemma":"orumai","gloss":"sole rule"},{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"person"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"ku","gloss":"to"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even/also"}],"gloss":"even to those who have sole rule"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நடுநாள்","parts":[{"text":"நடு","lemma":"naṭu","gloss":"middle"},{"text":"நாள்","lemma":"nāḷ","gloss":"day"}],"gloss":"midnight"},{"surface":"யாமத்தும்","parts":[{"text":"யாமத்தும்","lemma":"யாமத்தும்","gloss":"in the midnight hour also"}],"gloss":"in the midnight hour also","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பகலும்","parts":[{"text":"பகல்","lemma":"pakal","gloss":"daytime"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"in the daytime also"},{"surface":"துஞ்சான்","parts":[{"text":"துஞ்சு","lemma":"tuñcu","gloss":"sleep"},{"text":"ஆன்","lemma":"āṉ","gloss":"he who does not"}],"gloss":"he who does not sleep"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கடுமா","parts":[{"text":"கடு","lemma":"kaṭu","gloss":"swift/fierce"},{"text":"மா","lemma":"mā","gloss":"beast/animal"}],"gloss":"swift beast"},{"surface":"பார்க்கும்","parts":[{"text":"பார்க்கும்","lemma":"பார்க்கும்","gloss":"watching"}],"gloss":"watching","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கல்லா","parts":[{"text":"கல்","lemma":"kal","gloss":"learn"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"not (negative)"}],"gloss":"unlearned"},{"surface":"ஒருவற்கும்","parts":[{"text":"ஒருவன்","lemma":"oruvaṉ","gloss":"one person"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"ku","gloss":"to"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"to a person also"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உண்பது","parts":[{"text":"உண்","lemma":"uṇ","gloss":"eat"},{"text":"பது","lemma":"patu","gloss":"that which is"}],"gloss":"that which is eaten"},{"surface":"நாழி","parts":[{"text":"நாழி","lemma":"nāḻi","gloss":"a measure of grain"}],"gloss":"one measure of grain"},{"surface":"உடுப்பவை","parts":[{"text":"உடு","lemma":"uṭu","gloss":"wear"},{"text":"பவை","lemma":"pavai","gloss":"those which are"}],"gloss":"garments worn"},{"surface":"இரண்டே","parts":[{"text":"இரண்டு","lemma":"iraṇṭu","gloss":"two"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"two indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பிறவும்","parts":[{"text":"பிற","lemma":"piṟa","gloss":"other things"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"other things also"},{"surface":"எல்லாம்","parts":[{"text":"எல்லாம்","lemma":"ellām","gloss":"all"}],"gloss":"all"},{"surface":"ஓரொக்குமே","parts":[{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"one/same"},{"text":"ஒக்கும்","lemma":"okkum","gloss":"resembles/is equal"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"are exactly the same indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அதனால்","parts":[{"text":"அதனால்","lemma":"அதனால்","gloss":"therefore"}],"gloss":"therefore","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"செல்வத்துப்","parts":[{"text":"செல்வத்துப்","lemma":"செல்வத்துப்","gloss":"of wealth"}],"gloss":"of wealth","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பயனே","parts":[{"text":"பயன்","lemma":"payaṉ","gloss":"benefit/fruit"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"the benefit indeed"},{"surface":"ஈதல்","parts":[{"text":"ஈ","lemma":"ī","gloss":"give"},{"text":"தல்","lemma":"tal","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"giving/sharing"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"துய்ப்பேம்","parts":[{"text":"துய்","lemma":"tuy","gloss":"enjoy/consume"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"p","gloss":"future tense marker"},{"text":"பேம்","lemma":"pēm","gloss":"we (first person plural)"}],"gloss":"we will enjoy/consume"},{"surface":"எனினே","parts":[{"text":"எனின்","lemma":"eṉiṉ","gloss":"if one says/thinks"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"if one thinks so"},{"surface":"தப்புந","parts":[{"text":"தப்பு","lemma":"tappu","gloss":"miss/fail/be lost"},{"text":"ந","lemma":"na","gloss":"neuter plural suffix"}],"gloss":"those that are lost"},{"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"pala","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"are many indeed"}]}],"literal":"Clear sea surrounded world, without common ownership, / white umbrella shading, even to those of sole rule, / middle of the night hour also, and day also, without sleeping, / swift beast watching, even to an unlearned person, / that which is eaten is one measure, those worn are two indeed, / other things all are exactly the same indeed. / Therefore, of wealth the benefit indeed is giving. / 'We will enjoy' if one thinks so, those that are lost are many indeed.","translation":"Even for a great king who rules the entire world surrounded by the clear sea as his sole domain under his white umbrella, and for an unlearned hunter who does not sleep day or night as he watches for swift prey, the food eaten is but a single measure, and the garments worn are only two. All other basic needs are exactly the same. Therefore, the true purpose of wealth is to give to others; if one hoards it thinking 'I alone shall enjoy it,' much of it will only be lost.","modern":"தெளிந்த கடலால் சூழப்பட்ட இவ்வுலகத்தை, பிறருக்குப் பொதுவானது என்று இல்லாமல், தன் ஒருவனுக்கே உரியதாக வெண்கொற்றக் குடையின் கீழ் ஆளும் மன்னனுக்கும்; நள்ளிரவிலும் பகலிலும் தூங்காமல், விரைந்து ஓடும் விலங்குகளை வேட்டையாடக் காத்திருக்கும் கல்லாத வேடனுக்கும்; உண்ணும் உணவு ஒரு நாழி அளவே ஆகும், உடுத்தும் ஆடைகள் இரண்டே ஆகும். மற்ற தேவைகள் யாவும் இருவருக்கும் சமமே. ஆதலால், செல்வத்தைச் சேர்ப்பதன் பயன் பிறருக்குக் கொடுப்பதே ஆகும். அவ்வாறு கொடுக்காமல், 'நாமே எல்லாவற்றையும் அனுபவிப்போம்' என்று எண்ணினால், அச்செல்வத்தில் அழியக் கூடியவை பலவாகும்.","explanation":"The poet, Maturaik Kaṇakkāyaṉār Makaṉār Nakkīraṉār, offers a profound philosophical reflection on the equality of human needs and the true purpose of wealth. He compares a mighty emperor who rules the entire world under his white umbrella with an uneducated hunter who stays awake day and night to catch wild beasts. Despite their vast difference in status, both consume only a single measure of food and wear only two pieces of clothing. The contrast between the grand white umbrella of the king and the sleepless hunter highlights the universality of basic human limitations. The poem belongs to the potuviyal tiṇai and poruṇmoḻikkāñci theme, teaching that since physical needs are limited, the only true value of wealth lies in giving to others.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.6],[0.6,1.2],[1.2,1.6],[1.6,2.6],[2.6,3.0],[3.0,3.1],[3.1,3.4],[3.4,4.8],[4.8,4.8],[4.8,5.7],[5.7,5.8],[5.8,7.2],[7.2,7.2],[7.2,7.6],[7.6,7.9],[7.9,9.2],[9.2,9.3],[9.3,9.8],[9.8,9.9],[9.9,11.3],[11.3,11.5],[11.6,11.8],[11.8,12.2],[12.2,13.1],[13.1,13.5],[13.5,14.0],[14.0,14.0],[14.0,15.2],[15.2,15.3],[15.3,15.7],[15.7,16.2]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.7],[0.7,1.5],[1.5,1.6],[1.6,2.8],[2.8,3.3],[3.3,3.4],[3.4,3.8],[3.8,5.1],[5.1,5.2],[5.2,6.1],[6.1,6.1],[6.1,7.5],[7.5,7.5],[7.5,7.9],[7.9,8.3],[8.3,9.6],[9.6,9.8],[9.8,10.3],[10.3,10.4],[10.4,11.7],[11.7,12.0],[12.13,12.27],[12.4,12.55],[12.7,13.6],[13.6,14.0],[14.0,14.6],[14.6,14.7],[14.7,15.08],[15.08,15.08],[15.08,17.0],[17.0,17.1]]},"sync":[[["தெண்கடல்","clear sea"]],[["வளாகம்","expanse/world"]],[["பொதுமை","common ownership"]],[["இன்றி","without"]],[["வெண்குடை","white royal umbrella"]],[["நிழற்றிய","that shaded"]],[["ஒருமையோர்க்கும்","even to those who have sole rule"]],[["ஒருமையோர்க்கும்","even to those who have sole rule"]],[["நடுநாள்","midnight"]],[["யாமத்தும்","in the midnight hour also"]],[["பகலும்","in the daytime also"]],[["துஞ்சான்","he who does not sleep"]],[["கடுமா","swift beast"]],[["பார்க்கும்","watching"]],[["கல்லா","unlearned"]],[["ஒருவற்கும்","to a person also"]],[["உண்பது","that which is eaten"]],[["நாழி","one measure of grain"]],[["உடுப்பவை","garments worn"]],[["இரண்டே","two indeed"]],[["பிறவும்","other things also"]],[["எல்லாம்","all"]],[["ஓரொக்குமே","are exactly the same indeed"]],[["ஓரொக்குமே","are exactly the same indeed"]],[["அதனால்","therefore"]],[["செல்வத்துப்","of wealth"]],[["பயனே","the benefit indeed"]],[["ஈதல்","giving/sharing"]],[["துய்ப்பேம்","we will enjoy/consume"]],[["எனினே","if one thinks so"]],[["தப்புந","those that are lost"]],[["பலவே","are many indeed"]]]}